      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "HIGHLAND KITTY (5) is in good touch and hard to look past, having won her Ipswich Mdn by just under three lengths and placed three times from three attempts at this track and distance. Can go on with the job now. POUTCHEK (6) is the main danger after just missing here last time over the 1800m when sent out favourite. The first try at 2200m is the obvious query, but expecting her to handle it on the quick turnaround. TARADALE (2) was a sound second in CL3 company at Ipswich at generous odds, with his prior BM65 fourth adding substance. EVADE THE GAME (4) has been close enough in stronger company at this venue and strips rock-hard fit in this lesser grade. Worth keeping in mind.",
